        "text": "<p><strong>What’s the difference between Max Relief and Relief?</strong><br/>Both topicals offer similar strength, but they serve different needs. Max Relief is best for targeted relief and deeper discomfort because it includes a natural hot-and-cooling sensation that activates quickly and supports pain relief. Relief contains no hot or cooling ingredients, making it ideal for use near sensitive areas. Relief is also great for full-body massage, daily muscle tension, and overall comfort.<br/><br/><strong>Will the topicals get me high?</strong><br/>No. Our topicals do not produce intoxicating or psychoactive effects. They work locally on the area where they are applied.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Will I fail a drug test if I use your topicals?</strong><br/>Our topicals contain less than 0.3 percent THC per milligram, which is the legal limit for hemp products and is extremely unlikely to affect a drug test. Because topicals work locally on the skin and do not enter the bloodstream the same way ingestible products do, they are not expected to trigger a positive result. However, testing standards and individual physiology vary, so we cannot guarantee outcomes for every person or testing method. If you undergo strict drug testing, consult your organization before use.</p>",
